<title>TURKEY: Turk Petrol Ofisi 96 profits up 163 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Petrol Ofisi 96 profits up 163 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   4,196.68  vs   1,598.29</p>
<p>    Net profit		   10,575.64  vs   4,027.69</p>
<p>    Net sales		   321,547.26  vs 147,476.42</p>
<p>    Operating profit	   17,174.49  vs   6,820.85</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  9,387.86  vs   5,685.69</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 6,258.36  vs   3,701.66</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		    0	vs	 0</p>
<p>    Total debts		  20,259.01  vs  10,393.62</p>
<p>    Equity			 16,722.47  vs   8,667.92</p>
<p>    Capital			 2,520.00  vs   2,520.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Largely state owned petroleum products and lubricants marketer Petrol Ofisi A.S. is slated for privatisation with 93.3 percent of its shares owned by Turkey's privatisation administration OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
